  "answer": "This looks like a known problem: after the Command Palette Dock gained per-monitor settings (0.100.x), it doesn't reliably handle monitor configuration changes such as docking or undocking a laptop. The settings page often lists only the internal monitor, and the dock can disappear or show up empty. The past tickets don't give a fix, and the issue is still open. The workaround you already found, turning Command Palette off and on again, is the best option. Restarting PowerToys also helped some users in a related ticket (PowerToys#49053). You can add your details to PowerToys#48516 to help the team track it."
 },
